                                                "sense_id": "077d7e08-ee25-3ada-b46c-2616fd3dfb40",
                                                "text": "New York, Ohio, and Texas ruled that transsex persons could marry only in the gender role that they had been assigned at birth."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "transsex",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc7daea9-1237-33fc-9779-d67ef81d4d50",
                                        "entry_id": "7cb97438-4b65-35ad-b3f6-6af9bb439640",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Transsexuality, transsexualism; the state of being transsexual. (Compare transgender.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "675a1201-c607-4bf5-a5d2-4ce4263c6f3e",
                                                "sense_id": "cc7daea9-1237-33fc-9779-d67ef81d4d50",
                                                "text": "Before we can answer this question, we need to consider two other phenomena – transsex and transgender – which also expose the muddle within conventional categories of sex."
